    "details": "<p>Most hackathons end with a demo. RevHack ends with real users.</p>\n<p>RevHack is a free, 36-hour online hackathon for students across India. You have 36 hours to build, then about a week to put it in front of real people and get your first users or sales. Build anything that can earn: a website for your side business, an app people love, a browser extension folks have always wished existed, or software that businesses will pay for.</p>\n<p><strong>Register on EYFI:</strong> <a href=\"https://revhack.eyfichallenge.com/register\">https://revhack.eyfichallenge.com/register</a><br />Registration is completed on the RevHack page. Joining on Unstop alone doesn&rsquo;t count. Registrations close 16 Oct, 11:59 PM IST.</p>\n<p><strong>Key dates (all IST)</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>16 Oct, 11:59 PM: registrations close</li>\n<li>17 Oct, 10:00 AM to 18 Oct, 10:00 PM: The Build (36 hours), with mentor check-ins and feedback. In the last 2 hours, other teams try out what you&rsquo;ve built, so you get real feedback.</li>\n<li>18 to 26 Oct: The Traction Run. Get users, land your first customers, and submit your traction details by 26 Oct.</li>\n<li>31 Oct: Results day</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Prizes worth ₹13.5K in cash and $900 in credits</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Podium awards: ₹7,500 for the winner and ₹3,500 for the runner-up.</li>\n<li>BuildInPublic Award: ₹2,500 for the most compelling build-in-public journey.</li>\n<li>Render Workflows credits: $500, $300 and $100 for the top three teams. If they use Render Workflows in their project.</li>\n<li>Free 1-year .xyz domains for the top 25 teams.</li>\n<li>Venture grants: products that gain real momentum and traction can apply for grants from a pool of up to ₹5,00,000. This is not a guaranteed prize, and eligibility is based on traction.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Who can join</strong><br />Students across India, solo or in teams. Open theme, as long as it can earn.</p>",
